IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa19-nouns`
IMPORT `coa19-a1-after`

-- coa19-tests-a1-after.l4: tests for coa19-a1-after.l4 (ss 859H to 859O) and for the helper `s 859H(1)(b) the thing was done by the last day of the period` of coa19-nouns.l4.
-- Every expected value is written from the text of the section named in the comment above it, not from the code's output.

§ `Tests: ss 859H to 859O`

§§ `the in-time helper (s 859H(1)(b), used by ss 859K, 860, 862, 871, 878, 880)`
-- done on the last day: in time; done the day after: out of time; not done and the last day has not passed: not yet decided; not done and it has passed: out of time.
#ASSERT `s 859H(1)(b) the thing was done by the last day of the period` (JUST (Date 22 1 2025)) (Date 22 1 2025) (Date 30 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859H(1)(b) the thing was done by the last day of the period` (JUST (Date 1 1 2025)) (Date 22 1 2025) (Date 30 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859H(1)(b) the thing was done by the last day of the period` (JUST (Date 23 1 2025)) (Date 22 1 2025) (Date 30 1 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859H(1)(b) the thing was done by the last day of the period` NOTHING (Date 22 1 2025) (Date 22 1 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 859H(1)(b) the thing was done by the last day of the period` NOTHING (Date 22 1 2025) (Date 23 1 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 859H Consequence of failure to deliver charges`
-- (2) the relevant period: the period under the section in question, or if an order has been made under s 859F(3) the period it allows.
#ASSERT `s 859H(2) the last day of the relevant period allowed for delivery` (Date 22 1 2025) NOTHING EQUALS Date 22 1 2025
#ASSERT `s 859H(2) the last day of the relevant period allowed for delivery` (Date 22 1 2025) (JUST (Date 30 4 2025)) EQUALS Date 30 4 2025
-- (1) applies if a company creates a charge to which 859A or 859B applies and the documents were not delivered in time.
#ASSERT `s 859H(1) this section applies` TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859H(1) this section applies` FALSE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859H(1) this section applies` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859H(1) this section applies` FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859H(1) this section applies` TRUE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3) void against a liquidator, an administrator and a creditor; any other person is not decided.
#ASSERT `s 859H(3) the charge is void against the party` (JUST TRUE) `s 859H(3)(a) a liquidator of the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859H(3) the charge is void against the party` (JUST TRUE) `s 859H(3)(b) an administrator of the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859H(3) the charge is void against the party` (JUST TRUE) `s 859H(3)(c) a creditor of the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859H(3) the charge is void against the party` (JUST TRUE) `s 859H(3) any other person` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 859H(3) the charge is void against the party` (JUST FALSE) `s 859H(3)(c) a creditor of the company` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859H(3) the charge is void against the party` NOTHING `s 859H(3)(c) a creditor of the company` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4) without prejudice to the contract or obligation for repayment; the money immediately becomes payable when the charge becomes void.
#ASSERT `s 859H(4) subsection (3) prejudices the contract or obligation for repayment of the money secured by the charge` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859H(4) subsection (3) prejudices the contract or obligation for repayment of the money secured by the charge` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 859H(4) the money secured by the charge immediately becomes payable` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859H(4) the money secured by the charge immediately becomes payable` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859H(4) the money secured by the charge immediately becomes payable` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 859I Entries on the register`
#ASSERT `s 859I(1) this section applies` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859I(1) this section applies` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859I(2)(a) the registrar must allocate a unique reference code and place a note in the register` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859I(2)(a) the registrar must allocate a unique reference code and place a note in the register` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859I(2)(a) the registrar must allocate a unique reference code and place a note in the register` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2)(b) the six listed documents; any other is not decided
#ASSERT `s 859I(2)(b) the registrar must include the document in the register` (JUST TRUE) `s 859I(2)(b) a document delivered under section 859A(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859I(2)(b) the registrar must include the document in the register` (JUST TRUE) `s 859I(2)(b) a document delivered under section 859A(5)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859I(2)(b) the registrar must include the document in the register` (JUST TRUE) `s 859I(2)(b) a document delivered under section 859B(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859I(2)(b) the registrar must include the document in the register` (JUST TRUE) `s 859I(2)(b) a document delivered under section 859B(4)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859I(2)(b) the registrar must include the document in the register` (JUST TRUE) `s 859I(2)(b) a document delivered under section 859B(7)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859I(2)(b) the registrar must include the document in the register` (JUST TRUE) `s 859I(2)(b) a document delivered under section 859C(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859I(2)(b) the registrar must include the document in the register` (JUST TRUE) `s 859I(2)(b) any other document` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 859I(2)(b) the registrar must include the document in the register` (JUST FALSE) `s 859I(2)(b) a document delivered under section 859A(3)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859I(2)(b) the registrar must include the document in the register` NOTHING `s 859I(2)(b) a document delivered under section 859A(3)` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3) the certificate goes to the person who delivered the statement
#ASSERT `s 859I(3) the registrar must give the person a certificate of the registration of the charge` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859I(3) the registrar must give the person a certificate of the registration of the charge` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 859I(3) the registrar must give the person a certificate of the registration of the charge` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859I(3) the registrar must give the person a certificate of the registration of the charge` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4) the certificate states the registered name and number and the unique reference code
#ASSERT `s 859I(4) the certificate must state the item` `s 859I(4)(a) the registered name and number of the company in respect of which the charge was registered` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859I(4) the certificate must state the item` `s 859I(4)(b) the unique reference code allocated to the charge` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859I(4) the certificate must state the item` `s 859I(4) anything else` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5) signed by the registrar or authenticated by the official seal
#ASSERT `s 859I(5) the certificate is signed or authenticated as the subsection requires` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859I(5) the certificate is signed or authenticated as the subsection requires` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859I(5) the certificate is signed or authenticated as the subsection requires` FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859I(5) the certificate is signed or authenticated as the subsection requires` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (6) conclusive evidence, in the case of registration under 859A or 859B only
#ASSERT `s 859I(6) the certificate is conclusive evidence that the documents were delivered before the end of the relevant period` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859I(6) the certificate is conclusive evidence that the documents were delivered before the end of the relevant period` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 859I(6) the certificate is conclusive evidence that the documents were delivered before the end of the relevant period` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (7)
#ASSERT `s 859I(7) the last day of the relevant period allowed for delivery` (Date 22 1 2025) NOTHING EQUALS Date 22 1 2025
#ASSERT `s 859I(7) the last day of the relevant period allowed for delivery` (Date 22 1 2025) (JUST (Date 30 4 2025)) EQUALS Date 30 4 2025

§§ `s 859J Company holding property or undertaking as trustee`
#ASSERT `s 859J(1) the person may deliver to the registrar a statement that the company is acting as trustee` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859J(1) the person may deliver to the registrar a statement that the company is acting as trustee` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 859J(1) the person may deliver to the registrar a statement that the company is acting as trustee` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2) a statement delivered after the delivery for registration must include the name and number and the reference code
#ASSERT `s 859J(2) the statement must include the item` TRUE `s 859J(2)(a) the registered name and number of the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859J(2) the statement must include the item` TRUE `s 859J(2)(b) the unique reference code allocated to the charge` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859J(2) the statement must include the item` TRUE `s 859J(2) anything else` EQUALS NOTHING
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 859J(2) the statement must include the item` FALSE `s 859J(2)(b) the unique reference code allocated to the charge` EQUALS JUST FALSE; s 859J(2): a statement that is not a later statement is outside the class the duty is laid on, so NOTHING; a duty limited by its own wording does not give the text's no outside the limit
#ASSERT `s 859J(2) the statement must include the item` FALSE `s 859J(2)(b) the unique reference code allocated to the charge` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 859K Registration of enforcement of security`
-- (1) a person obtains an order or appoints a receiver or manager under powers in an instrument
#ASSERT `s 859K(1) subsection (2) applies` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859K(1) subsection (2) applies` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859K(1) subsection (2) applies` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (8) applies only to a receiver or manager appointed by a court in England and Wales or Northern Ireland, or under an instrument governed by their law
#ASSERT `s 859K(8) this section applies to the receiver or manager` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859K(8) this section applies to the receiver or manager` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859K(8) this section applies to the receiver or manager` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (9) does not apply to a receiver appointed under Chapter 2 of Part 3 of the Insolvency Act 1986
#ASSERT `s 859K(9) this section applies to the receiver` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859K(9) this section applies to the receiver` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1), (8), (9) together
#ASSERT `s 859K(1), (8) and (9) the person must give notice to the registrar` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859K(1), (8) and (9) the person must give notice to the registrar` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859K(1), (8) and (9) the person must give notice to the registrar` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859K(1), (8) and (9) the person must give notice to the registrar` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859K(1), (8) and (9) the person must give notice to the registrar` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2)(a) within 7 days of the order or of the appointment: order on 1 March 2025, last day 8 March 2025
#ASSERT `s 859K(2)(a) the person gave the registrar notice within 7 days` (Date 1 3 2025) (JUST (Date 8 3 2025)) (Date 20 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859K(2)(a) the person gave the registrar notice within 7 days` (Date 1 3 2025) (JUST (Date 9 3 2025)) (Date 20 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859K(2)(a) the person gave the registrar notice within 7 days` (Date 1 3 2025) NOTHING (Date 8 3 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 859K(2)(a) the person gave the registrar notice within 7 days` (Date 1 3 2025) NOTHING (Date 9 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2)(b): by virtue of a registered charge held by the person: a charge created before 6 April 2013 needs the subsection (4) information, not the reference code
#ASSERT `s 859K(2)(b) the notice to the registrar must contain the item` TRUE (Date 5 4 2013) `s 859K(4)(a) the date of the creation of the charge` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859K(2)(b) the notice to the registrar must contain the item` TRUE (Date 5 4 2013) `s 859K(4)(b) a description of the instrument (if any) creating or evidencing the charge` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859K(2)(b) the notice to the registrar must contain the item` TRUE (Date 5 4 2013) `s 859K(4)(c) short particulars of the property or undertaking charged` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859K(2)(b) the notice to the registrar must contain the item` TRUE (Date 5 4 2013) `s 859K(2)(b)(ii) the unique reference code allocated to the charge` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a charge created on 6 April 2013 or later needs the reference code, not the subsection (4) information
#ASSERT `s 859K(2)(b) the notice to the registrar must contain the item` TRUE (Date 6 4 2013) `s 859K(2)(b)(ii) the unique reference code allocated to the charge` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859K(2)(b) the notice to the registrar must contain the item` TRUE (Date 6 4 2013) `s 859K(4)(a) the date of the creation of the charge` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859K(2)(b) the notice to the registrar must contain the item` TRUE (Date 1 1 2020) `s 859K(4)(c) short particulars of the property or undertaking charged` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not by virtue of a registered charge held by the person: paragraph (b) does not apply
#ASSERT `s 859K(2)(b) the notice to the registrar must contain the item` FALSE (Date 1 1 2020) `s 859K(2)(b)(ii) the unique reference code allocated to the charge` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859K(2)(b) the notice to the registrar must contain the item` TRUE (Date 1 1 2020) `s 859K anything else` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3) on ceasing to act
#ASSERT `s 859K(3) the person must, on so ceasing, give the registrar notice` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859K(3) the person must, on so ceasing, give the registrar notice` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859K(3)(b) the notice to the registrar must contain the item` (Date 5 4 2013) `s 859K(4)(a) the date of the creation of the charge` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859K(3)(b) the notice to the registrar must contain the item` (Date 5 4 2013) `s 859K(2)(b)(ii) the unique reference code allocated to the charge` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859K(3)(b) the notice to the registrar must contain the item` (Date 6 4 2013) `s 859K(2)(b)(ii) the unique reference code allocated to the charge` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859K(3)(b) the notice to the registrar must contain the item` (Date 6 4 2013) `s 859K(4)(b) a description of the instrument (if any) creating or evidencing the charge` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859K(3)(b) the notice to the registrar must contain the item` (Date 6 4 2013) `s 859K anything else` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5) the registrar includes the facts notified under (2)(a) and (3)(a)
#ASSERT `s 859K(5) the registrar must include the fact in the register` `s 859K(5)(a) a fact of which notice is given under subsection (2)(a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859K(5) the registrar must include the fact in the register` `s 859K(5)(b) a fact of which notice is given under subsection (3)(a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859K(5) the registrar must include the fact in the register` `s 859K(5) any other fact` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (6) the offence: a person who makes default in complying with (2) or (3)
#ASSERT `s 859K(6) the person commits an offence` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 859K(6) the person commits an offence` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859K(6) the person commits an offence` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 859K(6) the person commits an offence` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (7) the penalty: on summary conviction, level 3, and a daily default fine of one-tenth of level 3
#ASSERT (`s 859K(7) the penalty for the offence`'s `how convicted`) EQUALS `on summary conviction`
#ASSERT (`s 859K(7) the penalty for the offence`'s `fine not exceeding`) EQUALS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1)
#ASSERT (`s 859K(7) the penalty for the offence`'s `daily default fine for continued contravention`) EQUALS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1)
#ASSERT (`s 859K(7) the penalty for the offence`'s `imprisonment not exceeding`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 859K(7) the penalty for the offence`'s `imprisonment and fine together`))
-- the pounds a level stands for is an input: with level 3 at 1,000 the fine is at most 1,000 and the daily default fine 100 (illustrative figures supplied by the test)
#ASSERT `s 859K(7) the most in pounds that the fine limit allows` (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1) 1000 5000 EQUALS JUST 1000
#ASSERT `s 859K(7) the most in pounds that the fine limit allows` (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1) 1000 5000 EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `s 859K(7) the most in pounds that the fine limit allows` (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1) 1000 5000 EQUALS JUST 5000
#ASSERT `s 859K(7) the most in pounds that the fine limit allows` (`a fine without a stated limit`) 1000 5000 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 859K(7) the most in pounds that the fine limit allows` (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 4 1) 1000 5000 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 859K(7) the most in pounds that the fine limit allows` (`a fine not exceeding an amount in pounds` 250) 1000 5000 EQUALS JUST 250

